It’s tucked between a vape shop and a frozen-yogurt place.

Purple curtain. Neon moon in the window. Sign says:

PALM • TAROT • AURA • PAST LIVES
$25 WALK-INS

Jessica sees it first.

“No.”

Cage stops walking.

“I haven’t said anything.”

“You stopped.”

“I’m reading.”

“You’re locking on.”

Little Nick is already climbing out of Cage’s coat pocket.

“Could be useful.”

Jessica points at him.

“You especially shut up.”

Micro Nick peers around the lapel.

“Threshold.”

Cage’s eyes widen.

“Exactly.”

Jessica: “HE SAID ONE WORD.”

