Celeste pulls out the tarot deck.

“Would you like three cards?”

Cage:

“How many exist?”

“Seventy-eight.”

“I’ll take seventy-eight.”

“No.”

“Why?”

“Because I have another appointment.”

Cage looks wounded.

“Destiny has a scheduling conflict?”

Celeste sighs.

“Three cards.”

She shuffles.

Cage watches the deck like he suspects it of insider trading.

She lays down the first card.

THE FOOL.

Jessica starts laughing immediately.

Cage looks at her.

“Immature.”

Little Nick: “It’s a strong opener.”

Celeste says, “The Fool represents beginnings. A leap into the unknown.”

Cage nods.

“Correct.”

Jessica: “You broke into a museum because a churro fell on a receipt.”

Cage: “Unknown.”

⸻

Second card.

THE TOWER.

Little Nick leans back.

“Damn.”

Celeste: “Sudden disruption. Collapse. Revelation.”

Cage narrows his eyes.

“Structural failure?”

“Symbolically.”

“Could it be literal?”

“Usually no.”

Micro Nick whispers:

“Usually.”

Cage immediately points at him.

“Thank you.”

Jessica: “DO NOT VALIDATE HIM.”

⸻

Third card.

Celeste flips it.

Stops.

Looks at Cage.

Then at the card.

Then back at Cage.

THE MOON.

Nobody says anything.

Little Nick slowly takes off his tiny sunglasses.

Jessica:

“…Okay, that’s admittedly annoying.”

Cage leans forward.

“The moon.”

Celeste nods.

“Uncertainty. Illusion. Dreams. Things hidden beneath appearances.”

Cage:

“Or jurisdiction.”

Celeste:

“What?”

Little Nick:

“Don’t worry about it.”

Cage is now completely gone.

Not crazy-gone.

National Treasure gone.

He points at the spread.

“The Fool. The Tower. The Moon.”

Celeste: “Yes.”

Cage:

“Journey. Collapse. Lunar jurisdiction.”

“That is not what I said.”

“But it’s what you meant.”

“No.”

“Subconsciously?”

“No.”

“Archetypally?”

“…maybe.”

Cage SLAMS both hands on the table.

“WE’RE IN.”

Jessica:

“IN WHAT?”

Cage:

“I don’t know yet.”

