He stands on the cards.

Looks down.

Points.

One card is slightly misaligned.

Cage pulls it out.

It’s blank.

Just white cardstock.

Celeste frowns.

“I don’t have blank cards.”

Little Nick:

“Okay.”

Jessica:

“No, no, no. Cards get misprinted.”

Cage:

“Or unwritten.”

Jessica:

“DON’T.”

Micro Nick touches the blank card.

A tiny black dot appears in the center.

Everyone watches.

The dot slowly becomes a line.

The line becomes a word:

CAGE.

Celeste stands up.

“I’m closing.”

Cage:

“What does it mean?”

“I don’t care.”

Jessica:

“Finally, somebody with boundaries.”

Celeste grabs her purse.

“Take the deck.”

Cage:

“I couldn’t.”

“TAKE IT.”

Little Nick is already putting it into his miniature backpack.

“Acquired.”

