Jessica:

“So what did we learn?”

Cage thinks.

Long pause.

Then:

“That palmistry is interpretive, tarot is probabilistic, symbolism is recursive, and Debra gives an excellent layered bob.”

Jessica:

“That’s actually reasonable.”

Cage:

“And the Moon Cop sequel is real.”

“There it is.”

Little Nick climbs onto his shoulder.

“What now?”

Cage looks down the street.

Across the road is another neon sign:

PSYCHIC • PET COMMUNICATION • $40

Cage freezes.

Jessica sees it.

“Nick.”

He says nothing.

“Nick.”

His eyes lock onto the sign.

Little Nick whispers:

“Razzmatazz.”

Jessica:

“DON’T YOU FUCKING SAY THE CAT’S NAME.”

Cage is already crossing the street.

“WE HAVE QUESTIONS.”

Micro Nick, from his pocket:

“Many.”

Jessica follows, furious.

Behind them, Madame Celeste flips the CLOSED sign.

Then notices one tarot card left on the table.

She turns it over.

It’s a picture of Big Nick.

Eleven feet tall.

Santa hat.

Holding a moon.

At the bottom:

THE MANAGEMENT.

